			"notes": "**Unofficial** modded build of Anubis 0.9.9.1 by **4ldenz**, from the `anubis-modded` branch. Not affiliated with or endorsed by the original author. GPL-3.0-only.\n\n> **Pre-release:** the new Base Finder compiles and builds, but hasn't been tested in-game yet. Detection thresholds may need tuning.\n\n## What's new: Base Finder\nA new module in the **Base Finding** category. It combines several signals into one ranked list:\n- Players hiding underground (live, remembered for a configurable time)\n- Player storage, crafted blocks, redstone, placed lights and building blocks buried below the surface\n- Rotated deepslate, which natural generation never produces\n- Hand-mined tunnels (straight 1x2) and shafts (1x1), deep underground\n- Grown amethyst and kelp, plus long dripstone, which only grow while players keep a chunk loaded\n- False positives from strongholds, ancient cities, trial chambers, dungeons, ruined portals and monuments are suppressed\n\nFlagged chunks get a soft tile at the depth of the evidence and a dot. Aim at the dot to see why it was flagged. A top-left panel ranks the most likely chunks with distance and direction.\n\nOriginal implementation; no code from Prestige or the Glazed addon.\n\n## Requirements\n- Minecraft **1.21.11**, Fabric Loader **0.16.0+**, **Fabric API**\n\n## Checksum\n`anubis-0.9.9.1+mc1.21.11-modded.jar` SHA-256: `007cd14f5021dd354f31e2e65c6687d70c87eaef9174c0d78e9afc6bc925f51f`\n\nBuilt from commit 1adb931 on `anubis-modded`."
